 "D_interpretation": "A = gamma * residence time measures the growth, during the packet's stay in the high-curvature region, of a perturbation seeded at entry in an unstable Killing-time mode. The mode is a global bound state of the TEST FIELD: a toy instability (tachyonic xi R coupling), NOT the instability of the source of the benchmark. For the forced phantom source no growth rate is derived here (literature: unstable radial mode, not recomputed)."
